Would the hon. member allow me to ask a question? Does he not agree it is normal procedure to pass the interpretation clause at the beginning and then, if there is anything in it that would not make sense later, following some substantive amendment of another clause, to return to the interpretation clause and make appropriate alterations? This is the way it is always done and it does not preclude the committee from dis-20220-735}
Canada Pension Plan
cussing all the clauses and moving all the amendments it wishes.
